\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The evaluation family. Intervention scores: $\phi _{\mathrm  {ind}}$ sufficiency to induce, $\phi _{\mathrm  {sup}}$ necessity; ``set'' means set to activating-context values. Faithfulness $\phi ^{\mathrm  {free}}_{\pi }$ measures whether the circuit reproduces the target alone with its nodes recomputed, clamped faithfulness $\phi ^{\mathrm  {pin}}$ whether it contains the right latents, and each variant names its ablation method $\pi $ (Z zero, A mean over activating contexts, C mean over contrast contexts; sp sparsity-preserving; \cref  {sec:problem}). The $\alpha $ rows score weighted circuits with their scaling coefficients applied (\cref  {sec:weighted}). SAE errors are preserved in every row, and every ratio reads the target the same way in all of its terms (\cref  {app:protocol}).}}{6}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:semantics}{{1}{6}{The evaluation family. Intervention scores: $\phiind $ sufficiency to induce, $\phisup $ necessity; ``set'' means set to activating-context values. Faithfulness $\phi ^{\mathrm {free}}_{\pi }$ measures whether the circuit reproduces the target alone with its nodes recomputed, clamped faithfulness $\phi ^{\mathrm {pin}}$ whether it contains the right latents, and each variant names its ablation method $\pi $ (Z zero, A mean over activating contexts, C mean over contrast contexts; sp sparsity-preserving; \cref {sec:problem}). The $\alpha $ rows score weighted circuits with their scaling coefficients applied (\cref {sec:weighted}). SAE errors are preserved in every row, and every ratio reads the target the same way in all of its terms (\cref {app:protocol})}{table.1}{}}
